{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1039294-is-there-really-only-one-way-to-make-a-scion","id":1039294,"title":"Is there really only one way to make a Scion?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-28T00:14:26-08:00","id":1039294,"title":"Is there really only one way to make a Scion?","content":"I haven't had a chance to out 2e yet so please tell me if they brought this up there. Scions are made the same way humans are- a sperm and an egg meet up, compare notes and get replicating. Most often this comes from a sexual fling between a god and a mortal that leaves the mortal holding a baby and a grudge. Some times the divine parent donates their end of the bargain, some times they pretend to be the mortal's significant other or sometimes the mortal worships the divine parent, but somewhere in the deal egg, sperm, BOOM! But the gods have a history of creating heroic characters in a multitude of ways. Why not make Scions in these ways?<br /> <br /> Why couldn't a Scion character have started out as a normal human (or maybe an humanized animal) who impressed a god and was patronized. Why couldn't a god make a scion out of a storm or a solar flair. Maybe one of the major gods could curse a lesser god to mortality and they have to work their way back to godhood from hero status. And there's certainly no shortage of artifacts that can imbue divine powers to their wielders. <br /> <br /> Have any of you tried any of these methods of character creation or one that I haven't mentioned in your games? What do you think about these suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12923-brian-orcus","name":"Brian Orcus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T00:26:55-08:00","id":1039297,"title":"","content":"We're getting more ways of making Scions in 2e - the core will have, in addition to born Scions, Scions who were created and Scions who were chosen as infants. Scions who are reincarnations of dead heroes / gods are slated for somewhere later in the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T00:32:29-08:00","id":1039298,"title":"","content":"Cool. Can a Scion be made out of something like river water? And if so, does that make them their own birthright? As in, because they're made of water they have the ability to control it in their own flesh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12923-brian-orcus","name":"Brian Orcus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T00:42:10-08:00","id":1039302,"title":"","content":"Been experimenting with shinto last 2 or 3 years.<br /> <br /> Can someone become a Scion through Misogi? <br /> <br /> sounds COOL to me.<br /> <br /> it suggests in some books ive read that is the true purpose of Misogi shuho, to return to ones original divine Kami Nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T01:11:33-08:00","id":1039305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian Orcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1039294-is-there-really-only-one-way-to-make-a-scion?p=1039298#post1039298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool. Can a Scion be made out of something like river water? And if so, does that make them their own birthright? As in, because they're made of water they have the ability to control it in their own flesh?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only real requirement we have for the Created material-wise is that they're made from inanimate materials I could see a river water Scion arising from the water, or being a transformed river, or being something like Momotaro, found in something floating in the water.<br /> <br /> Created get a different starting Knack and Genesis Knack list - Knacks in 2e have been removed from Attributes and focused on divine archetypes and archetypal images. What that means is there may be a Knack reflecting the Scion's water-born origin, and if not you could create one.<br /> <br /> Dunno whether you could be your own Birthright, but being born of a river is certainly a good argument for taking the Water Purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T01:18:32-08:00","id":1039307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1039294-is-there-really-only-one-way-to-make-a-scion?p=1039302#post1039302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Been experimenting with shinto last 2 or 3 years.<br /> <br /> Can someone become a Scion through Misogi?<br /> <br /> sounds COOL to me.<br /> <br /> it suggests in some books ive read that is the true purpose of Misogi shuho, to return to ones original divine Kami Nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the purposes of the game, mortal apotheosis requires a spark from the divine. That said, mortals do have other options - there's been mention of holy figures/saints.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T01:24:39-08:00","id":1039311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1039294-is-there-really-only-one-way-to-make-a-scion?p=1039305#post1039305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only real requirement we have for the Created material-wise is that they're made from inanimate materials I could see a river water Scion arising from the water, or being a transformed river, or being something like Momotaro, found in something floating in the water.<br /> <br /> Created get a different starting Knack and Genesis Knack list - Knacks in 2e have been removed from Attributes and focused on divine archetypes and archetypal images. What that means is there may be a Knack reflecting the Scion's water-born origin, and if not you could create one.<br /> <br /> Dunno whether you could be your own Birthright, but being born of a river is certainly a good argument for taking the Water Purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really need to get the PDF. So a Scion couldn't be made for an animal or a plant. Too bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12923-brian-orcus","name":"Brian Orcus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T01:40:18-08:00","id":1039312,"title":"","content":"Plants aren't a problem - the example Created for the alpha slice was carved from a living ash tree.<br /> <br /> 2e's still in development, with the Origins and Hero PDFs expected later this year. Most of the info we have is from what the developer and writers have said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T02:15:17-08:00","id":1039320,"title":"","content":"Still sucks that an animal can't be made a Scion. Imagine how much fun that sort of character would be. Sure a Scion can become an animal, but it just isn't the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12923-brian-orcus","name":"Brian Orcus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T03:04:33-08:00","id":1039332,"title":"","content":"No official word on animals yet, though it has been pointed out that Loki's kids include the siblings Hel, Fenris and the Midgard Serpent, which would point to the possibility of animals being born or chosen Scions...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T05:54:48-08:00","id":1039390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian Orcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1039294-is-there-really-only-one-way-to-make-a-scion?p=1039311#post1039311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really need to get the PDF. So a Scion couldn't be made for an animal or a plant. Too bad.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hey... Wonder Woman was sculpted out of clay and struck by a lightning bolt. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1039294-is-there-really-only-one-way-to-make-a-scion?p=1039332#post1039332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No official word on animals yet, though it has been pointed out that Loki's kids include the siblings Hel, Fenris and the Midgard Serpent, which would point to the possibility of animals being born or chosen Scions...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about Hel, but at least Fenris and Jormagandur were sired with a giantess, not a mortal woman.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian Orcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1039294-is-there-really-only-one-way-to-make-a-scion?p=1039320#post1039320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still sucks that an animal can't be made a Scion. Imagine how much fun that sort of character would be. Sure a Scion can become an animal, but it just isn't the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is disappointing, actually. Considering that there are religions throughout history that worshiped animals as such. Hell, just look at the Egyptian pantheon; more than half of them are some kind of animal-human hybrid! And in Shinto, there are hundreds (thousands?) of lesser Kami who resemble animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-28-2017, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T07:31:09-08:00","id":1039413,"title":"","content":"When did I say animals couldn't be or be made into Scions? You could do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T07:40:07-08:00","id":1039414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1039294-is-there-really-only-one-way-to-make-a-scion?p=1039413#post1039413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When did I say animals couldn't be or be made into Scions? You could do that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Squee! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Now I'm trying to imagine how you'd go about playing an animal character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T08:43:27-08:00","id":1039432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1039294-is-there-really-only-one-way-to-make-a-scion?p=1039390#post1039390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about Hel, but at least Fenris and Jormagandur were sired with a giantess, not a mortal woman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hel was born to the same mother as Fenris and Jormagundr.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T11:15:54-08:00","id":1039520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1039294-is-there-really-only-one-way-to-make-a-scion?p=1039413#post1039413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When did I say animals couldn't be or be made into Scions? You could do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my house-setting, Bast was originally a cat Scion of Sekhmet who grew to assume one of her mother's spare Mantles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T11:20:30-08:00","id":1039522,"title":"","content":"Deleted post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T16:50:19-08:00","id":1039681,"title":"","content":"The question is whether a scion made from an animal would still have animal shape or even animal intelligence or if it would be transformed into a human or antromorph. Playing anyone of those character types would be lot of fun and an interesting role play challenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12923-brian-orcus","name":"Brian Orcus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T17:06:40-08:00","id":1039692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian Orcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1039294-is-there-really-only-one-way-to-make-a-scion?p=1039681#post1039681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question is whether a scion made from an animal would still have animal shape or even animal intelligence or if it would be transformed into a human or antromorph. Playing anyone of those character types would be lot of fun and an interesting role play challenge.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Things would be... problematic if it had the power of a god, but an animal's intelligence.<br /> <br /> Fenrir is depicted as having the body of a feral wolf, yet somehow retains the capacity for speech. He was able to challenge the gods to feats of strength and bargain Tyr's hand when they managed to successfully bind him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-28-2017, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T18:18:46-08:00","id":1039723,"title":"","content":"I don't know. If a cat was given the ability to shoot fire and an understanding of how to use that power it would probably use it the same as claws. If said cat was being bossed around by Bast-et it would have something specific to do with it. There are plenty of creatures in Scion that lack human intelligence but have god like powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12923-brian-orcus","name":"Brian Orcus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T19:35:03-08:00","id":1039752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian Orcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1039294-is-there-really-only-one-way-to-make-a-scion?p=1039681#post1039681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question is whether a scion made from an animal would still have animal shape or even animal intelligence or if it would be transformed into a human or antromorph. Playing anyone of those character types would be lot of fun and an interesting role play challenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Turned human,&quot; &quot;shapeshifter,&quot; and &quot;just a dog, but also a demigod&quot; are all viable options.<br /> <br /> &quot;Animal-level intelligence,&quot; not really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T19:35:04-08:00","id":1039753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian Orcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1039294-is-there-really-only-one-way-to-make-a-scion?p=1039681#post1039681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question is whether a scion made from an animal would still have animal shape or even animal intelligence or if it would be transformed into a human or antromorph. Playing anyone of those character types would be lot of fun and an interesting role play challenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Turned human,&quot; &quot;shapeshifter,&quot; and &quot;just a dog, but also a demigod&quot; are all viable options.<br /> <br /> &quot;Animal-level intelligence,&quot; not really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T04:48:31-08:00","id":1039928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian Orcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1039294-is-there-really-only-one-way-to-make-a-scion?p=1039298#post1039298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool. Can a Scion be made out of something like river water? And if so, does that make them their own birthright? As in, because they're made of water they have the ability to control it in their own flesh?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I recall correctly a scion gets one of their parent's purviews as innate and don't need a birthright for it. So as long as your river scion was made by a water deity then they could totally be their own birthright.<br /> <br /> Again, assuming I'm remembering that part of the ask Neil thread correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T05:39:26-08:00","id":1039944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1039294-is-there-really-only-one-way-to-make-a-scion?p=1039928#post1039928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I recall correctly a scion gets one of their parent's purviews as innate and don't need a birthright for it. So as long as your river scion was made by a water deity then they could totally be their own birthright.<br /> <br /> Again, assuming I'm remembering that part of the ask Neil thread correctly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is that for second edition? Because in first, you only get innate purviews when you're a God, and even then, only if your mastery is level 8 or higher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T06:02:45-08:00","id":1039955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1039294-is-there-really-only-one-way-to-make-a-scion?p=1039944#post1039944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Is that for second edition? Because in first, you only get innate purviews when you're a God, and even then, only if your mastery is level 8 or higher.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, it is; everybody gets one innate purview that comes from their divine parent; I believe it was mentioned (don't recall if was from Neall or just fan-theory though) that Eric Donner inherited the Epic Strength purview from Thor, but then gains access to the Sky purview via Giantsbane","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T06:08:29-08:00","id":1039956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ffanxii4ever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1039294-is-there-really-only-one-way-to-make-a-scion?p=1039955#post1039955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, it is; everybody gets one innate purview that comes from their divine parent; I believe it was mentioned (don't recall if was from Neall or just fan-theory though) that Eric Donner inherited the Epic Strength purview from Thor, but then gains access to the Sky purview via Giantsbane</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Epic Attributes are a purview, now?<br /> <br /> Still, I like this idea, since mythical heroes and the like didn't always need artifacts to manifest their abilities. There was one Scion of Hera (forgot his name) who was practically invincible as long as he was in physical contact with the earth. <i>Basically meaning the entire planet was his birthright.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Also, imagining a child with the innate Justice purview. That's got to be hard for any parent trying to instill them with obedience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T06:38:43-08:00","id":1039961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ffanxii4ever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1039294-is-there-really-only-one-way-to-make-a-scion?p=1039955#post1039955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, it is; everybody gets one innate purview that comes from their divine parent; I believe it was mentioned (don't recall if was from Neall or just fan-theory though) that Eric Donner inherited the Epic Strength purview from Thor, but then gains access to the Sky purview via Giantsbane</div> </div> </div> </div>Eric got Forge as his innate purview.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1039294-is-there-really-only-one-way-to-make-a-scion?p=1039956#post1039956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Epic Attributes are a purview, now?</div> </div> </div> </div>The three physical Attributes are. The others have been dropped, using other methods such as Callings to replicate them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T16:32:31-08:00","id":1040281,"title":"","content":"<b>Animal Path: C\u00fa Sith</b><br /> <i>What? You've never seen a talking dog before?</i><br /> It doesn't matter what they call you\u2014Barghest, Church Grim, Gabriel's Ratchet, or simply Black Dog\u2014you are a prize of the Tuatha D\u00e9 Danann. You are faithful, yes, but you are also a warning of their displeasure and an omen of death. The gifts they've given you separate you from the common hounds of the World, a thing you take pride in: dogs know and fear you, but have no more intelligence than children compared to you. It can be lonely to see so many and be like so few.<br /> What you do have is your pack. They may be scattered, but they will come when you call for them, just as you will go to them when they need you. You'll cross the world to help them, and whether it's to fight, mate, or just to be with others of your kind, they will never turn on you.<br /> <b>Relationships:</b> packmates, devotees of the Tuatha D\u00e9 Danann, local dogs<br /> <b>Asset Skills:</b> Athletics, Survival<br /> <b>Innate Ability:</b> You can speak as well as any human.<br /> <b>Knacks:</b> Any one Hunter knack, Terrifying Howl (Custom knack), Call the Pack (Custom knack), Imperfect Disguise (white fur and red eyes; Antagonist drawback)<br /> <i>Terrifying Howl:</i> Howling for more than one action has supernatural effects. On the second action you <b>use to howl</b>, the sound can be heard for a mile around you. On the third action, treat it as the Immobilize Antagonist knack.<br /> <i>Call the Pack:</i> Once per session, you can <b>summon the spirits of your packmates </b>to you (if they are not physically present) and direct them against one enemy for a single attack. Treat them as a weapon with the Lethal, Loud, and Ranged tags, using Presence + Close Combat for the attack roll.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T09:57:02-08:00","id":1040733,"title":"","content":"But the all important question is, are they a good boy? That weighty question lies in the hands of notoriously untrustworthy players","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T22:57:33-08:00","id":1041113,"title":"","content":"A Scion of Poseidon, who was made from an octopus. I would name them <b>Tentacles</b> (pronounced Tenta-kleez, and meant to be a pun on Hercules)<br /> <br /> <br /> A Scion of Hades, carved out of the rocks of the Underworld itself. I would name them <b>Vrachos</b> (Rock), or <b>Theiafi </b>(Brimstone)<br /> <br /> <br /> A Scion of Zeus, he was immaculately conceived by Zeus's pent up frustrations during a particularly lengthy siege on Olympus. I would name them <b>Mataiosi </b>(Frustration), or <b>Lagneia </b>(Lust)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T03:08:41-08:00","id":1041166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1039294-is-there-really-only-one-way-to-make-a-scion?p=1041113#post1041113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Scion of Poseidon, who was made from an octopus. I would name them <b>Tentacles</b> (pronounced Tenta-kleez, and meant to be a pun on Hercules)<br /> <br /> <br /> A Scion of Hades, carved out of the rocks of the Underworld itself. I would name them <b>Vrachos</b> (Rock), or <b>Theiafi </b>(Brimstone)<br /> <br /> <br /> A Scion of Zeus, he was immaculately conceived by Zeus's pent up frustrations during a particularly lengthy siege on Olympus. I would name them <b>Mataiosi </b>(Frustration), or <b>Lagneia </b>(Lust)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes I wonder if he even remembers he has a wife. Then again he's probably been on the couch for like three or four thousand years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T07:17:35-08:00","id":1041243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreepyShutIn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1039294-is-there-really-only-one-way-to-make-a-scion?p=1041166#post1041166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sometimes I wonder if he even remembers he has a wife. Then again he's probably been on the couch for like three or four thousand years.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe it was a shotgun wedding and Zeus was never ready to settle down?<br /> <br /> The historians may have decided to omit that version of events in favor of a more respectable story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T13:11:49-08:00","id":1041431,"title":"",